    test(install): share the load-tolerant subprocess budget file-wide (QA-TERMINAL-JAIL-15)
    
    Follow-up to 63c1c17, which fixed the briefed helper only. Two further
    starvation events landed in the same hour on this host, both outside it:
    
    - _run_checkout_install (30s) starved at loadavg 31, failing
      test_rules_bak_retention_capped on a single install call (its 8 installs cost
      ~28s each at that load).
    - a jail CLI invocation starved at 20s, failing
      test_installed_binary_blocks_with_shipped_bridge while the same test had
      passed in the neighbouring suite run minutes earlier.
    
    The stall distribution for one identical install command, back to back, is
    0.14s / 59.41s / 6.22s at loadavg 35, and a 90s budget was itself exceeded once
    at loadavg 32.7 — so no fixed 15/20/30s ceiling survives this host's fleet-load
    spikes, and 90s was not enough either.
    
    One constant, honestly named, now covers every subprocess.run in this file that
    passes a timeout: SUBPROCESS_TIMEOUT_S (renamed from INSTALL_TIMEOUT_S), default
    180s (~3x the largest observed stall), overridable per host with
    TERMINAL_JAIL_TEST_TIMEOUT. That is all 32 sites — install.sh round trips plus
    the jail CLI and loader runs — because on this host each of them can stall for
    tens of seconds while its idle cost is sub-second. The 15/20/30s literals are
    gone from the file. The two subprocess.run sites with no timeout (sha256sum,
    `sh -n`) are unbounded already and are untouched. Test-only change; no product
    code touched.
    
    Verification (host loadavg 17-24):
    - call-site probe: SUBPROCESS_TIMEOUT_S == 180 and both installer helpers hand
      timeout=180 to subprocess.run; TERMINAL_JAIL_TEST_TIMEOUT=7 -> timeout=7
    - AST check over the file: 32/32 timeout-bearing subprocess.run sites use the
      constant, 0 literal budgets left
    - the previously starved CLI test plus the rule-pack family (both rule-pack-file
      tests, the checkout-refusal test, the broken-pack chain, and
      test_rules_bak_retention_capped): 6 passed in 184.66s
    - plugin/ suite: 1504 passed, 7 skipped, rc=0 (263.65s)
    - full testpaths suite (plugin + tests): 1558 passed, 7 skipped, rc=0 (479.08s)
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
